{
  "summary": "Exposes the node's `interfaces::Chain` over IPC using Cap'n Proto proxy wrappers, split into a stable `Chain` interface and an `UnstableChain` interface. The stable interface covers basic block lookups for external clients under Cap'n Proto backward-compatibility rules, while `UnstableChain` exposes the remaining methods for internal Bitcoin Core consumers. It also updates the `src/ipc/libmultiprocess` subtree and makes minor adjustments to `interfaces::Chain` method signatures to support code generation.",
  "problem": "Processes connecting to `bitcoin-node` over IPC via `-ipcbind` cannot read chain data or follow chain notifications, blocking multiprocess wallet separation (#10102). Exposing the entire raw `interfaces::Chain` C++ interface to external IPC clients would freeze internal wallet APIs against future refactoring.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Processes connected to bitcoin-node over IPC (with -ipcbind) can use the Mining interface, but they can't currently use the Chain interface read chain data or follow chain events. Chain data could be useful to third-party clients and Bitcoin Core's own wallet could use this as well to run in a separate process (#10102).'",
    "PR description references #34981 ('multiprocess: expose existing interfaces or design new ones?') as the rationale for splitting into stable and unstable interfaces."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36520"
    ],
    "enables": [
      "#10102",
      "#19460",
      "#19461"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Carries an update to the src/ipc/libmultiprocess subtree accounting for the majority of changed files and commits, alongside new Cap'n Proto schema and wrapper files. Also includes minor signature adjustments in src/interfaces/chain.h (removing const qualification from two estimation methods and passing updateRwSetting callbacks by value).",
  "changed_since_previous": "The bundled libmultiprocess subtree update was refreshed with upstream changes including v14 platform support and CI updates, and a compiler flag was added to suppress -Wc++23-lambda-attributes warnings.",
  "card": "Exposes the Chain interface over IPC using Cap'n Proto, splitting it into a version-stable Chain interface with basic block lookup methods and an UnstableChain interface for Bitcoin Core internal consumers. Currently, chain data and notifications are inaccessible over IPC, blocking multiprocess wallet separation (#10102) and external clients connecting via -ipcbind. This is a core prerequisite for running the wallet in an isolated process (#19460) and depends on #36520.",
  "needs": [],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "medium",
    "touches": [
      "wallet",
